  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.104,
            0.319,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ARITHMETIC PROGRESSIONS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.873,
            0.105,
            0.898,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "51"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.139,
            0.902,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the examples above, we observe some patterns. In some, we find that the succeeding terms are obtained by adding a fixed number, in other by multiplying with a fixed number, in another we find that they are squares of consecutive numbers, and so on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.222,
            0.903,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this chapter, we shall discuss one of these patterns in which succeeding terms are obtained by adding a fixed number to the preceding terms. We shall also see how to find their nth terms and the sum of n consecutive terms, and use this knowledge in solving some daily life problems."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.313,
            0.409,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.2 Arithmetic Progressions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.338,
            0.484,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the following lists of numbers :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.364,
            0.305,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) 1, 2, 3, 4, . . ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.388,
            0.36,
            0.409
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) 100, 70, 40, 10, . . ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.414,
            0.364,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) – 3, –2, –1, 0, . . ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.439,
            0.305,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) 3, 3, 3, 3, . . ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.464,
            0.405,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) –1.0, –1.5, –2.0, –2.5, . . ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.49,
            0.608,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Each of the numbers in the list is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "term",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.515,
            0.902,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Given a term, can you write the next term in each of the lists above? If so, how will you write it? Perhaps by following a pattern or rule. Let us observe and write the rule."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.573,
            0.66,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In (i), each term is 1 more than the term preceding it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.597,
            0.665,
            0.618
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In (ii), each term is 30 less than the term preceding it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.623,
            0.782,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In (iii), each term is obtained by adding 1 to the term preceding it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.648,
            0.902,
            0.688
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In (iv), all the terms in the list are 3 , i.e., each term is obtained by adding (or subtracting) 0 to the term preceding it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.692,
            0.902,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In (v), each term is obtained by adding – 0.5 to (i.e., subtracting 0.5 from) the term preceding it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.734,
            0.902,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In all the lists above, we see that successive terms are obtained by adding a fixed number to the preceding terms. Such list of numbers is said to form an "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Arithmetic Progression ( AP )",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.797,
            0.902,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "an arithmetic progression is a list of numbers in which each term is obtained by adding a fixed number to the preceding term except the first term.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.859,
            0.902,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This fixed number is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "common difference",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the AP. Remember that it "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "can be positive, negative or zero",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.983
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
